{:edb/db-before-t 595 :edb/db-after-t 596 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533908 50 #inst "2026-10-05T11:01:29.799Z" 13194139533908 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265088 13194139533908 true] [17592186105829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265098 13194139533908 true] [17592186105830 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265095 13194139533908 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265081 13194139533908 true] [17592186105831 1020 #edb/ref 17592186265102 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265082 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1089 "q-161104" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/059cec995f7ef75b56b8c512af09051fe4631733e87d98d25065144500613f73.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $17{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $△BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1113 #uuid "d8ed3010-dff4-51a2-aca7-aa8cacfdb425" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265081 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 63\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{46}^{∘} \\\\  & =22.659… \\\\  & ≈23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =23-17 \\\\  & =6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265083 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265084 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265085 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265086 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265087 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1041 "selection" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265087 13194139533908 true] [17592186265082 1110 #uuid "dea223c9-b378-5277-809b-3aa4514f3aef" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265083 1034 "5{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265083 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265083 1111 #uuid "3b81cd48-3354-5858-9ebe-421ee2b6c885" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265084 1034 "8{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265084 1111 #uuid "8b6dcf4d-86a9-57c8-b277-0fcc4540b956" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265085 1034 "4{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265085 1111 #uuid "11e038a3-1182-54b8-b86e-6fe72b888668" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265086 1034 "7{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265086 1111 #uuid "8b83ad97-c460-53f0-9e14-da679cb42406" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265087 1034 "6{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265087 1111 #uuid "85afa586-798a-5cb1-bdba-502fe874a14e" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265089 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1089 "q-161109" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b95571772af958b4f7b7dcdbba630b78e029c838340dc272809a6c7915dc9c90.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1113 #uuid "3f5486d5-f842-5cab-abfe-caf15b80d4f5" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265088 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=6\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{21\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265090 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265091 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265092 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265093 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265094 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1041 "selection" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265091 13194139533908 true] [17592186265089 1110 #uuid "156f3f94-c03f-5e25-846d-ab87c7a8f0ae" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265090 1034 "6\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265090 1111 #uuid "d99ce202-bf1b-59b0-9790-dc8037fbdc7e" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265091 1034 "7\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265091 1111 #uuid "912c8688-c2f9-51d1-b753-42c7c7830a6a" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265092 1034 "7.5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265092 1111 #uuid "f6d0fa2c-295e-5aaa-ae81-010af2790b7a" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265093 1034 "6.5\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265093 1111 #uuid "97682d06-c845-592f-9f69-d2a728b91a58" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265094 1034 "8\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265094 1111 #uuid "aa985a76-a9b9-5b69-840b-0742526df5af" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265096 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1089 "q-279762" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/54265327c77bedb300fe0d1f1f08ca3ab2d7ae37f35f49007d3f20ab3a21dbaa.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1113 #uuid "7534130c-7b66-543d-b26d-a4a7b4a429a1" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265095 1145 "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b1d0cf7c5a7c6ad7f0f52c8686239920fabcb05be57372ae0c7c9c9491838a52.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)(6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈25.981,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 25.981 \\\\  & =51.962.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $52.$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265097 13194139533908 true] [17592186265096 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533908 true] [17592186265096 1041 "field-1" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265096 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265097 13194139533908 true] [17592186265096 1110 #uuid "709258f2-84c2-5384-b559-2a3be2dd0ec4" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265097 1034 "52" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265097 1111 #uuid "fdc387d7-8c8c-581a-a9d6-703f80eb0fc9" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265099 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1089 "q-280282" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/5c0bf3060129e2a03dab0fcd2a6f0f6068d1ec565143b83d11ad4d8ae1b41b85.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1113 #uuid "f42a4731-18b0-562d-a10b-9dc0dd292374" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265098 1145 "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{ mm}, \\\\ b & =AC=4\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265100 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265101 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1041 "field-1" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265100 13194139533908 true] [17592186265099 1110 #uuid "fa7aff40-0fe9-5c3f-a695-745f3d50bfb6" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265100 1034 "60" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265100 1111 #uuid "55db0fbe-c27d-5d05-b585-851aa55b2dc5" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265101 1034 "30" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533908 true] [17592186265101 1111 #uuid "0ab95a5b-1a0f-5c4b-b9e3-6d0cd5cc5526" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265103 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1089 "q-285740" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951536/assets/b69082ef86283bc842ce487b62901e8946ffff53ab8323a6fc846f68c5869aae.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $10{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1113 #uuid "4c12c505-999a-5051-95ac-753d9f8950cf" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265102 1145 "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘} \\\\  & =11.591… \\\\  & ≈12{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533908 true] [17592186265103 1000 #edb/ref